# Decouple Runner from UI Implementation Details

## Context

The `run_with_ui` method in `src/runner/workflow.rs` has several direct dependencies on UI implementation details that bypass the `UserInterface` trait abstraction:

1. **`BivvyTheme` instantiated directly** (line 317) — used for formatting step headers, skipped/blocked status messages throughout the method
2. **`indicatif::ProgressBar` leaked through `SpinnerHandle` trait** — `fn progress_bar()` returns an `Option<ProgressBar>`, coupling any consumer to the `indicatif` crate
3. **`live_output_callback` imported from `ui::spinner`** (line 19) — runner creates output callbacks that depend on `indicatif::ProgressBar`
4. **Direct `println!` in runner** (line 626) — for non-interactive verbose output streaming, instead of going through the UI

## Approach

Add higher-level methods to `UserInterface` and `SpinnerHandle` so the runner expresses *what* it needs without knowing *how* the UI renders it.

## Changes

### 1. `src/ui/mod.rs` — Trait changes

**`UserInterface` trait** — add three methods with defaults:

```rust
fn format_step_display(&self, name: &str, title: &str, index: usize, total: usize) -> String {
    // Default: plain "[1/7] name — title" (or "[1/7] name" when name == title)
}

fn format_status(&self, kind: StatusKind, message: &str) -> String {
    // Default: "○ Skipped (reason)" using StatusKind::format_plain
}

fn create_line_callback(&self, _indent: usize) -> Option<crate::shell::OutputCallback> {
    None
}
```

**`SpinnerHandle` trait** — replace `progress_bar()`:

```rust
// REMOVE:
fn progress_bar(&self) -> Option<ProgressBar> { None }

// ADD:
fn create_output_callback(&self, base_message: String, indent: usize, max_lines: usize)
    -> Option<crate::shell::OutputCallback> { None }
```

Remove `use indicatif::ProgressBar` from `mod.rs`.

### 2. `src/ui/terminal.rs` — `TerminalUI` implementations

```rust
fn format_step_display(&self, name: &str, title: &str, index: usize, total: usize) -> String {
    // Use self.theme.step_number, step_title, dim — same logic currently in workflow.rs:359-374
}

fn format_status(&self, kind: StatusKind, message: &str) -> String {
    kind.format(&self.theme, message)
}
```

### 3. `src/ui/non_interactive.rs` — `NonInteractiveUI` implementations

```rust
fn format_step_display(...) -> String {
    // Plain: "[1/7] name — title"
}

fn format_status(&self, kind: StatusKind, message: &str) -> String {
    kind.format_plain(message)
}

fn create_line_callback(&self, indent: usize) -> Option<crate::shell::OutputCallback> {
    if self.mode == OutputMode::Verbose {
        let prefix = " ".repeat(indent);
        Some(Box::new(move |line| { ... println!("{prefix}{text}") ... }))
    } else {
        None
    }
}
```

### 4. `src/ui/mock.rs` — `MockUI` implementation

```rust
fn format_step_display(...) -> String {
    // Plain formatting (same as default impl)
}

fn format_status(&self, kind: StatusKind, message: &str) -> String {
    kind.format_plain(message)
}
```

### 5. `src/ui/spinner.rs` — `ProgressSpinner` changes

Replace `progress_bar()` with `create_output_callback()`:

```rust
fn create_output_callback(&self, base_message: String, indent: usize, max_lines: usize)
    -> Option<crate::shell::OutputCallback>
{
    Some(live_output_callback(self.bar.clone(), base_message, indent, max_lines))
}
```

Keep `live_output_callback` as a crate-private function (remove `pub`). Update its existing tests (they call it directly, which is fine since they're in the same module).

Remove `progress_bar()` from `ProgressSpinner`.

Update spinner tests: replace `progress_bar_returns_clone` and `hidden_spinner_progress_bar_returns_some` with tests for `create_output_callback`.

### 6. `src/runner/workflow.rs` — Remove coupling

Remove imports:
```rust
// REMOVE:
use crate::ui::spinner::live_output_callback;
use crate::ui::theme::BivvyTheme;
```

Remove `StatusKind` from the import (no longer needed in runner).

Replace `let theme = BivvyTheme::new();` and all theme-based formatting:

- `theme.format_skipped(msg)` → `ui.format_status(StatusKind::Skipped, msg)` — wait, we removed StatusKind. Actually, let's keep StatusKind in the runner imports. It's a data enum, not an implementation detail. The coupling problem is the *theme formatting*, not the status enum itself.

Actually, re-evaluating: `StatusKind` is fine to keep in the runner — it's a domain concept (step status), not a UI implementation detail. The issue is calling `StatusKind::format(&theme, ...)` which requires a `BivvyTheme`. With `ui.format_status(kind, msg)`, the runner passes the enum to the UI and the UI handles formatting.

Changes in `run_with_ui`:

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `let theme = BivvyTheme::new();` | (remove) |
| `theme.format_skipped(&format!("..."))` | `ui.format_status(StatusKind::Skipped, "...")` |
| `StatusKind::Blocked.format(&theme, "...")` | `ui.format_status(StatusKind::Blocked, "...")` |
| Step display formatting (lines 359-374) | `ui.format_step_display(step_name, &step.title, index + 1, total)` |
| `spinner.progress_bar()` + `live_output_callback()` | `spinner.create_output_callback(...)` |
| `println!("      {text}")` callback | `ui.create_line_callback(6)` |

### 7. Tests

- **`src/ui/spinner.rs`**: Update `progress_bar_returns_clone` → test `create_output_callback` returns `Some`. Update `hidden_spinner_progress_bar_returns_some` → test hidden spinner returns `None` from `create_output_callback`.
- **`src/runner/workflow.rs`**: Existing tests use `MockUI` which will get default impls. No test changes needed — the behavior is the same, just the formatting path changed.
- Add a test in `src/ui/terminal.rs` for `format_step_display` and `format_status`.
- Add a test in `src/ui/mock.rs` for `format_step_display` and `format_status`.

## Files Modified

1. `src/ui/mod.rs` — trait changes
2. `src/ui/terminal.rs` — TerminalUI impls
3. `src/ui/non_interactive.rs` — NonInteractiveUI impls
4. `src/ui/mock.rs` — MockUI impls
5. `src/ui/spinner.rs` — ProgressSpinner changes, visibility of `live_output_callback`
6. `src/runner/workflow.rs` — remove BivvyTheme/live_output_callback coupling

## Verification

```sh
cargo test --all-features
cargo doc --no-deps --all-features
cargo fmt -- --check && cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo build --all-targets --all-features
cargo build --release
```

